WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.568
History unfolding at the U.S.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.402
Capitol today

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.170
with the January 6th Select Committees

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.939
announcement of four criminal referrals

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.140
against Donald Trump.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:07.941
The panel arguing

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:08.208
Trump

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:09.809
should never be allowed to serve

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.112
in a position of authority again.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:12.979
But in a new clip

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.114
played by the committee,

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.116
Trump's longtime aide and confidant

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:16.950
Hope Hicks

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.584
made it clear

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.052
that Trump's primary goal

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.221
has always been winning too expensive.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.055
Anything else?

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.790
Listen to her describe a conversation

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.691
she had with Trump

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.194
about his claims of voter fraud

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.731
being evidence of

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:36.269
fraud on a scale that would have impacted

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.804
the outcome of the election

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:38.471
and I was

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.940
becoming increasingly concerned that

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:46.312
we were damaging

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.215
we were damaging his legacy

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.316
say in response

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.585
to what you just described,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.055
he said something along the lines of

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:58.758
you know,

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.760
nobody will care about my legacy

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.063
if I lose

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.801
so that won't matter.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.403
The only thing that matters is,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.072
is winning

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:13.940
All right.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.608
So let's put some perspective and context

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:15.842
on this

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.010
with our team of veterans

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:17.744
from the Watergate

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.312
era, the legendary journalist

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:19.946
Bob Woodward

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.880
and Carl Bernstein

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.116
and the former Nixon White House counsel

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.684
John Dean.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:25.452
John, you know,

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.886
she said all he cared about was winning.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.188
And if he didn't win,

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.189
he'd have no legacy.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:32.058
Of course, now he does have a legacy.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.560
So what stands out to you

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.261
the most from what she said

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.429
and what we've learned today?

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.831
Well, what she said

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.566
is that he's going to have the wrong

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.533
legacy.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.302
Have the legacy of a loser

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.471
and that's not a legacy he can handle.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.839
What stood out to me

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.340
was the very beginning.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.775
The chairman,

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.009
in a passing remark

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.845
said what we're sending

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.613
to the Department of Justice

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.948
is a roadmap.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.516
Well, that just clicked right away

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.718
because during Watergate,

00:01:58.718 --> 00:01:59.752
it was just the reverse.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.387
The special prosecutors

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.590
sent the Congress a roadmap.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.658
So I think that's the way

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.360
they envision this document

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.962
and this material,

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.131
because they've been here much longer.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.365
Than the Department of Justice.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.867
They've been looking at this evidence.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.502
So I'm sure they're quite familiar

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.070
with where these roads go,

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.271
with where they go. Right.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.472
And all the all the transcripts

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.007
and backup information

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:21.674
that they have

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:22.375
that they haven't given

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.811
to the Department of Justice yet.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:25.979
What what do you think

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:26.980
is the most important thing

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.248
from what you've now seen?

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:31.584
Well, they're for referrals here.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.820
And I think the one that's important

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:38.458
is the one that says it is a crime

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:41.761
to subvert a lawful function

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.795
of government.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.198
In the lawful function of government

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.033
is where,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.235
according to the 12th Amendment

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.004
to the Constitution,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.972
the president of the Senate,

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.575
who in this case, Vice President

00:02:55.842 --> 00:03:00.246
Pence, oversees the counting of the votes

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.349
And I think the part of the evidence

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.419
that is most significant

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.122
legally and most reprehensible

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.825
is when Trump was pressuring Pence.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:16.162
Here's Trump, the boss, the subordinate.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.163
And he's saying,

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.798
you're not going to be my friend.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.234
You're a wimp. You're betraying us.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.736
And that

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.973
in just a normal case, with the boss

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.741
putting that kind of

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.944
pressure on a subordinate

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:33.880
is almost a crime in itself.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:34.647
And of course,

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.783
once you prove one of these,

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.650
they they each come

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.452
with multiple year sentences.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.420
But but anything would be

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.655
hugely significant, I mean, to say that.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.825
Yeah, but I think for people are going

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.026
to have to sort this out

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:48.962
just like the Justice Department.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.764
What's important, what's not important.

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:55.635
And I think this is the one and I

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.003
quite frankly,

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.538
think it will resonate

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.640
and it does resonate with people.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:01.207
I mean,

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:04.244
what's the president of the United States

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.679
talking to the vice president?

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.881
I'm not going to be your friend.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.716
We joke

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:10.483
that it's

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.585
as if Trump was saying the Pence.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:13.419
Yes.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.187
Next year,

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:15.388
I'm not going to invite you

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:18.057
to my birthday party at Mar a Lago.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.659
And people can understand that pressure.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:20.226
It makes sense.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:20.727
That's your point.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.161
If you're going to go ahead with charges

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:22.595
to go with.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:23.496
What people can truly

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:24.631
understand is in part,

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.365
this is a document

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.633
to convince the public.

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.268
Carl, John Eastman,

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.069
the lawyer, along with Donald J.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:30.903
Trump, is who

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:31.838
the committee is referring

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:32.605
for, both obstruction

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.340
of official proceeding and conspiracy

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.708
to defraud the United States.

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:37.510
Presumably also for the insurrection

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:38.578
and conspiracy charges.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.313
But he's in the end others there.

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.247
If so,

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.482
he has just responded saying

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.017
this is yet another

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:46.219
partizan and political stunt.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:47.520
That's the

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.222
first response that we have

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.090
to be expected.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.160
He is a principal conspirator

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:54.994
in what

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.562
today was outlined

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.399
as a absolute lutely, stunning

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:03.770
cancer, conspiracy to defraud

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.805
the United States to prevent

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:06.572
free election

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.141
of the president of the United States.

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:09.642
The transfer of power.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.177
But, you know, we started this

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:12.612
by talking about history.

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.113
And one of the things we've been asking,

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:16.683
is there another John Dean,

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.817
as from in Watergate,

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.919
somebody who can bring the house down?

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:22.021
And the answer is potentially yes.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.390
And we got a hint of it today.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.992
Pat Cipollone,

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:27.694
he is the counsel to the president

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:28.594
of the United States,

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.764
who in the hearings, we could see him hem

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:34.467
and haw as he took various privileges.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.437
However, he knows everything

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.672
Absolutely everything.

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:40.907
There is indications

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.342
he is cooperating

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:44.010
with the Justice Department.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.446
Those privileges might not apply.

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:48.748
So I think we better keep our eye

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:50.249
on that substantively

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.852
because it is really significant.

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.654
And I will just leave us on that

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:54.887
to say

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:55.988
the committee believes the White House

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:56.823
counsel, Pat Cipollone,

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.224
he gave a particularly important

00:05:58.224 --> 00:05:59.192
account of the events.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.460
They are patting him on the back

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.562
and making it clear that he was helpful.

